    "https://careers.widener.edu/en-us/job/493298/adjunct-digital-media-informatics": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Digital Media Informatics",
      "description": "Adjunct, Digital Media Informatics Apply now Job no: 493298 Work type: Adjunct Location: Chester Categories: Adjunct Widener University's College of Arts & Sciences, Digital Media Informatics Program is accepting applications for highly qualified Adjunct faculty to teach Introduction to Informatics (DMI 101) course in the Fall 2026 semester. Adjunct faculty is expected to teach a specified course as assigned; prepare course materials; and provide support and guidance to students. This course introduces students to the field of informatics and serves as a foundation course to the digital media informatics, business informatics, and health informatics majors. Through lecture and lab activities, students learn about the growth of computer technologies and their impact on the media and business in modern society. Students participate in several computer-based exercises. Key components of the course include an introduction and definition of informatics; computers and how they work; data and knowledge representation; business information systems; digital media technology; health care data systems; and computerized technology trends. Does not fulfill social science or science general education requirements. This is a writing-enriched course. No prerequisites. 3 semester hours Job Qualifications: Required: Master's Degree in Informatics, Business Administration, Management Information Systems, Digital Media, Digital Communication, Digital Marketing, Computer Science, Computer Information Systems, Business Informatics, Business Analytics or closely related majors and relevant industry/professional experience. For further information about the Digital Media Informatics program, please visit our website at https://www.widener.edu/academics/undergraduate-programs/digital-media-informatics-major Widener University is committed to fostering an inclusive community in which faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. Widener University, an independent, metropolitan, doctoral-intensive university, connects curricula to social issues through civic engagement. Dynamic teaching, active scholarship, personal attention and experiential learning are key components of the Widener Experience. Located in Chester, PA, Widener's main campus is nestled between Philadelphia, PA and Wilmington, DE, with Law Schools located in both Harrisburg and Wilmington. For more information about the university, please visit our website at www.widener.edu. EOE M/F/V/D Advertised: 23 Sep 2025 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.widener.edu/en-us/job/493278/shuttle-bus-driver-parttime": {
      "title": "Shuttle Bus Driver - Part-time",
      "description": "Shuttle Bus Driver - Part-time Apply now Job no: 493278 Work type: Part-time Location: Chester Categories: Staff Widener University is currently seeking a Part-Time Shuttle Bus Driver on our Chester campus. This role reports to the Assistant Director of Transportation and provides support to all faculty, students and staff across campus. The schedule for this role is part-time with some partial first and/or second shifts, Monday – Friday & possible weekends. Please note hours may vary. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (including, but not limited to) : Essential duties: Provide safe and professional shuttle service to the campus community and surrounding local areas Ability to operate 14 passenger vehicles Conduct pre- and post-trip vehicle safety inspections Maintain interior and exterior of vehicle to ensure safety and cleanliness, including daily sanitizing of common touch points throughout vehicle & a weekly thorough cleaning throughout flooring and seating areas Maintain service on assigned daily route and time schedule Comply with all state and federal rules and regulations, as well as University policies and procedures Maintain a friendly, helpful demeanor Monitor roadways and parking lot areas for potential hazards to vehicle and passengers Maintain accurate rider log as instructed Secondary responsibilities: Responsible to write and file reports as needed Ability to operate a radio or any equipment provided & located in vehicle Report all incidents or accidents immediately to the dispatch office and Supervisors as directed Perform other duties as assigned MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (education/training and experience required) : Required: High school graduate or equivalent Valid State Driver’s License with a clean driving record for past five (5) years Ability to operate vehicle in inclement weather Demonstrated ability to communicate tactically (written and verbal) with passengers and colleagues tactfully and effectively Superior interpersonal skills Ability to operate a computer, radio or equipment located in vehicle Ability to effectively manage time and prioritize Demonstrate organizational skills, attention to detail & accuracy Ability to work independently as well as in a team environment Ability to handle demanding situations professionally & tactfully Preferred: Previous professional experience in driving large groups Valid Commercial Driver’s License Familiarity with the local area and community Experience in a customer service-related role Experience working at a school or university PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND/OR UNUSUAL HOURS: May work weekends, holidays, nights, and special events Sitting in a vehicle for extended periods of time Ability to enter and exit vehicle as often as needed to assist passengers Ability and willingness to work in inclement weather Occasionally lift and carry items, up to 40 lbs. Ability to sit, stand, reach, kneel, squat and bend All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Widener University is committed to fostering an inclusive community in which faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. Widener University, an independent, metropolitan, doctoral-intensive university, connects curricula to social issues through civic engagement. Dynamic teaching, active scholarship, personal attention and experiential learning are key components of the Widener Experience. Located in Chester, PA, Widener's main campus is nestled between Philadelphia, PA and Wilmington, DE, with Law Schools located in both Harrisburg and Wilmington. For more information about the university, please visit our website at www.widener.edu. EOE M/F/V/D Advertised: 30 Jul 2025 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.widener.edu/en-us/job/493253/adjunct-instructor-english": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, English",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, English Apply now Job no: 493253 Work type: Adjunct Location: Chester Categories: Adjunct The Department of English and Creative Writing in the College of Arts and Sciences at Widener University invites applications for the position of adjunct professor of English (first-year writing). Applicants must have experience teaching first-year writing and be dedicated to working collaboratively in a department and university that values diversity. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (including, but not limited to) : Essential duties: Teaching one-three courses (depending on need) in Fall 2025 (ENGL 101 and/or introduction to literature courses, depending on need) Creating syllabi and assignments designed to hone writing, research, and critical thinking skills Emphasizing writing as a process through peer review, actionable feedback on drafts, student-instructor conferences, etc. Evaluating student work based on course goals Holding 4 office hours per week MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (e ducation/training and experience required) : Required: MA or above in English, Rhetoric/Composition, Creative Writing, or a related field. Experience teaching first-year writing courses at the college level (composition, literature surveys) All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Widener University is committed to fostering an inclusive community in which faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. Widener University, an independent, metropolitan, doctoral-intensive university, connects curricula to social issues through civic engagement. Dynamic teaching, active scholarship, personal attention and experiential learning are key components of the Widener Experience. Located in Chester, PA, Widener's main campus is nestled between Philadelphia, PA and Wilmington, DE, with Law Schools located in both Harrisburg and Wilmington. For more information about the university, please visit our website at www.widener.edu. EOE M/F/V/D Advertised: 09 May 2025 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
