    "https://careers.widener.edu/en-us/job/493448/assistant-teaching-professor-of-chemistry": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Chemistry Apply now Job no: 493448 Work type: Faculty (Non-tenure track) Location: Chester Categories: Faculty Reporting to the Dean of the College of Arts & Sciences, the Assistant Teaching Professor of Chemistry is a full-time, non tenure-track position beginning in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will have a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching. Teaching duties will include introductory chemistry courses and laboratories for both science/engineering majors and for non-science majors, including general, organic, and biochemistry for nursing students, as well as upper-level chemistry courses. Widener University is committed to fostering an environment in which faculty, staff, and students from diverse backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. The Chemistry Department places a high priority on inclusive pedagogy, mentoring, and community engagement. Candidates with experience working with diverse faculty, staff, and students who can contribute to an inclusive campus climate are encouraged to highlight these experiences in their application. The Chemistry Department is committed to creating an engaging learning environment. Our faculty employ active and collaborative learning approaches to help students develop strong conceptual understanding, problem-solving skills, critical thinking, and mastery of chemistry. We value close faculty-student interaction, continuous improvement in teaching, and a collaborative departmental culture. We are a proud signer of Beyond Benign’s Green Chemistry Commitment and are invested in the teaching of green chemistry across our curriculum. Experience in green chemistry is desirable. The reviewing process will start on January 11, 2027. For full consideration, qualified candidates must submit a cover letter, CV, and a teaching philosophy at widener.edu/jobs. Three confidential letters of reference and any additional related materials must be sent to artsandsciences@widener.edu. For more information about Widener University and the Department of Chemistry, see www.widener.edu . DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (including, but not limited to) : Essential duties: Teach Chemistry lecture and laboratory courses. Maintain regular weekly office hours to provide academic support and guidance to students enrolled in assigned courses. Service Attend division, College, and University faculty meetings and contribute to department initiatives. Secondary Responsibilities: Perform other job-related duties as assigned and participation in the intellectual life of the Department, the College of Arts & Sciences, and Widener University. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (education/training and experience required) : Required: A doctoral degree in chemistry or a closely related discipline. ABD candidates will be considered. Degree must be from an accredited University or College. Demonstrated experience teaching undergraduate chemistry courses. Preferred: Experience teaching organic chemistry. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage students and create an inclusive learning environment. Ability to work collaboratively with a diverse group of students and faculty. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND/OR UNUSUAL HOURS: Must be available for in-person instruction. Must be able to sit for extended periods while working at a computer or grading papers, and the ability to lecture in a classroom. Must have the ability to speak clearly and audibly to deliver lectures, facilitate classroom discussions and interact with students and colleagues. Must have the ability to move around campus to attend meetings and teach in different classrooms. Minimal lifting may be involved for tasks such as carrying materials to class or moving books. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Widener University is committed to fostering an inclusive community in which faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. U.S. work authorization is required. Widener University, an independent, metropolitan, doctoral-intensive university, connects curricula to social issues through civic engagement. Dynamic teaching, active scholarship, personal attention and experiential learning are key components of the Widener Experience. Located in Chester, PA, Widener's main campus is nestled between Philadelphia, PA and Wilmington, DE, with Law Schools located in both Harrisburg and Wilmington. For more information about the university, please visit our website at www.widener.edu. EOE M/F/V/D Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
