    "https://careers.widener.edu/en-us/job/493450/career-development-experiential-learning-coordinator-delaware-law-school": {
      "title": "Career Development & Experiential Learning Coordinator - Delaware Law School",
      "description": "Career Development & Experiential Learning Coordinator - Delaware Law School Apply now Job no: 493450 Work type: Full-time (hourly) Location: Delaware Categories: Staff Widener University Delaware Law School is currently seeking a Coordinator for the Career Development Office (CDO) and the Office of Experiential Learning (EL) in Wilmington, DE. Our mission is to provide our students and alumni with high-quality career counseling, services, and programming which will prepare them to succeed in a competitive marketplace. Reporting to the Assistant Dean of Career Development and Associate Dean of Experiential Learning at the Delaware Law School, the Career Development & Experiential Learning Coordinator plays a key role in advancing Delaware Law School’s mission by delivering high-quality career counseling, student and alumni services, and innovative programming designed to prepare graduates for success in a competitive legal marketplace. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (including, but not limited to) : Essential Duties: Career Development Office (CDO ): Monitor and respond to office email/phone calls from the courts, employers, and graduates. Coordinate all Job Posting services including internet research of potential job prospects, outreach to employers to promote services, and communication with employers to finalize listings of opportunities. Initiate recruitment of employers for on/off campus (OCI) programs, and process/approve employer job postings and registrations for job posting and OCI registrations in the Symplicity database. Facilitate the collection of student employment data for ABA compliance, maintain understanding of ABA employment reporting requirements, and perform entry of at- graduation and 10-month employment data into Symplicity database. Serve as subject-matter expert on Symplicity by establishing relationships with vendor contacts to maintain efficient use of CSM. Serve as point of contact and manage logistics for all on-campus CDO programs. Coordinate the 1L mentoring program including updating communications to invite potential mentors and mentees, facilitating matching of mentors with mentees, communicating matches to participants, and trouble-shooting and following up with mentors and mentees. Perform research to update employer contact information in Symplicity. Process student and alumni requests for reciprocity with other law school career development offices. Experiential Learning (EL ): Coordinate and organize student applications for experiential learning opportunities (clinics, externships & internships). Communicate with field placement supervisors to obtain written confirmation of internal and external field placements. Assist with the administration of Summer, Fall, and Spring EL programs including inviting potential field placements, processing registrations, following up with potential placements, ensuring receipt of student applications, and trouble-shooting interviewing (when applicable). Monitor and respond to office email/phone calls from field placement supervisors. Manage and maintain the collection of student experiential learning data (clinic and field placement engagement). Coordinate and perform research to update field placement contact information and application information. Draft emails to students promoting field placement opportunities in cooperation with our Career Development Office (CDO). Manage, develop, organize, and maintain departmental files. Secondary Responsibilities: Perform other job-related duties as assigned or directed to support departmental needs and align with the mission, values and goals of the Delaware Law School and Widener University. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (education/training and experience required) : Required: Associate’s degree. Three (3+) years of secretarial/administrative experience in an office environment supporting senior-level staff. An equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered. Professional presence to respond to first-level employer contacts with legal employers, Courts, alumni, law school faculty, and staff. Strong oral and written communication skills. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail; flexible and able to handle several tasks simultaneously. Ability to take initiative in order to complete projects in a timely fashion. Ability to comfortably navigate multiple technology platforms and to learn new platforms as required. Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite especially Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Preferred: Understanding of project management and/or event planning/coordination through work experience. Previous experience in law-related office, legal industry, or human resources. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND/OR UNUSUAL HOURS: Occasional standing, walking, or climbing stairs. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Widener University is committed to fostering an inclusive community in which faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. Some positions may be eligible for a hybrid or remote work arrangement that may include a partially or fully remote work location, consistent with Widener’s Flexible Work policy. Widener University, an independent, metropolitan, doctoral-intensive university, connects curricula to social issues through civic engagement. Dynamic teaching, active scholarship, personal attention and experiential learning are key components of the Widener Experience. Located in Chester, PA, Widener's main campus is nestled between Philadelphia, PA and Wilmington, DE, with Law Schools located in both Harrisburg and Wilmington. For more information about the university, please visit our website at www.widener.edu. EOE M/F/V/D Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.widener.edu/en-us/job/493449/ai-solutions-specialist": {
      "title": "AI Solutions Specialist",
      "description": "AI Solutions Specialist Apply now Job no: 493449 Work type: Full-time Location: Chester Categories: Administrators Widener University is currently seeking an AI Solutions Specialist. Reporting to the Vice President for Enrollment & Technology/Chief Information Officer, this newly created position will help the university’s administrative units put artificial intelligence to practical use, improving the speed and quality of the work that supports our students, faculty, and staff. The role will report directly to the Vice President while it is being established, then move into the Information Technology department. This is a hands-on role. The AI Solutions Specialist will work with units such as Admissions, Student Financial Services, the Registrar, Finance, Human Resources, Information Technology Services, etc. to identify high-value opportunities, then personally configure, test, deploy, and monitor the tools that address them. It is also strategic: the position maintains a university-wide view of where AI is and should be used, recommends what the university should license, and builds the training that equips staff to leverage these new tools. Qualified candidates will have both technological expertise and the interpersonal skills necessary to engage colleagues and campus stakeholders. Much of this work involves understanding how staff actually do their jobs and earning the trust required to manage change. The university is interested in what demonstrably works, not in adopting technology for its own sake. Duties and priorities will shift on an ongoing basis, so the successful candidate will bring comfort with ambiguity, a willingness to “figure it out,” and the autonomy to identify opportunities rather than wait for assignments. This position is eligible for regular remote/flex work, and the university will consider fully remote candidates; some on-campus presence may be expected during onboarding and periodically thereafter. Widener is committed to fostering an environment in which faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (including, but not limited to) : Essential Duties: Partner with administrative units to identify work that is repetitive, slow, error-prone, or backlogged, and assess honestly whether AI is the right tool. Configure, test, and deploy AI solutions hands-on: prompts, custom assistants and agents, document-grounded chat and search over a unit’s own content, drafting and summarization workflows, and extraction of structured data from forms and correspondence. Connect AI capabilities to existing university systems using workflow automation tools so that outputs land where staff already work. Monitor deployed solutions on a regular basis reviewing output quality, tracking adoption, catching degradation, and adjusting configuration as content, processes, and vendor capabilities change. Document configurations, prompts, and known limitations so that deployments are supportable and repeatable. Define and report success measures for each deployment (time saved, turnaround time, error rates, volume handled) and recommend retiring or rebuilding what does not deliver. In partnership with others, design and deliver practical training workshops, office hours, and role-specific guides that raises baseline AI fluency and builds capable practitioners in business units. Evaluate new tools, assess vendor claims critically, maintain a roadmap of AI use across administrative units, and report progress and priorities to university leadership. Ensure that every deployment adheres to university policy and applicable requirements for data security and privacy, record retention, and appropriate use. Secondary Responsibilities: Serve on division and campus-wide committees and participate in process improvement projects or strategic initiatives as assigned. Keep informed about developments in artificial intelligence, automation, and higher education technology, including relevant policies, regulations, and state and federal laws. Potential for modest supervisory responsibilities and/or collaboration opportunities with student employees or interns. Perform other job-related duties as assigned or directed to support departmental needs and align with the mission, values and goals of Enrollment & Technology and Widener University. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (education/training and experience required) : Required: Bachelor’s degree. Demonstrated hands-on experience building solutions with current generative AI tools (e.g., configuring custom assistants or agents, developing prompts for production use, or deploying document-grounded chat or retrieval over an organization’s own content). Working knowledge of at least one major enterprise AI platform (for example, Microsoft 365 Copilot, Google Gemini, ChatGPT Enterprise, or Anthropic Claude), including its administrative settings. Comfort working with data in spreadsheets and structured files, and an understanding of how systems exchange data through APIs. Ability to evaluate AI output critically recognizing hallucination, bias, and quiet failure and to build the checks that catch problems before end users do. Demonstrated ability to map a business process, identify where the friction actually lies, and design a change that staff will adopt. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, written and verbal, including the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical colleagues clearly and without condescension. Customer service orientation and ability to interact with a wide variety of individuals within a complex and dynamic environment. Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and organizational skills, with thoroughness and attention to detail. Ability to work independently, manage multiple projects, and prioritize among competing needs. Ability to identify gaps in one’s own knowledge and locate the resources to learn on one’s own, essential in a field changing this quickly. Formal software development experience is not required; candidates who have built practical solutions through configuration rather than code are encouraged to apply. Preferred: Master’s degree. Experience in higher education, or in another complex, decentralized organization. Experience delivering training or change management to non-technical staff. Familiarity with enterprise administrative systems such as Ellucian Colleague, Technolutions Slate, etc. Scripting ability (e.g., Python or JavaScript). SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS: Occasional travel to the university’s campuses will be required. This position may require vacation restrictions during times of peak activity in the department. The employee must have the ability to occasionally lift/or move 10+ pounds. The employee will perform repetitive motion using computer mouse and keyboard to type. Qualified candidates must submit resume and cover letter for consideration. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Only those selected to interview will be contacted. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Widener University is committed to fostering an inclusive community in which faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. Some positions may be eligible for a hybrid or remote work arrangement that may include a partially or fully remote work location, consistent with Widener’s Flexible Work policy. U.S. work authorization is required. Widener University, an independent, metropolitan, doctoral-intensive university, connects curricula to social issues through civic engagement. Dynamic teaching, active scholarship, personal attention and experiential learning are key components of the Widener Experience. Located in Chester, PA, Widener's main campus is nestled between Philadelphia, PA and Wilmington, DE, with Law Schools located in both Harrisburg and Wilmington. For more information about the university, please visit our website at www.widener.edu. EOE M/F/V/D Advertised: 19 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.widener.edu/en-us/job/493452/visiting-assistant-professor-of-nursing-nontenure-track": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Nursing - Non-tenure track",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Nursing - Non-tenure track Apply now Job no: 493452 Work type: Faculty (Non-tenure track) Location: Chester Categories: Faculty Widener University is currently seeking a Visiting Professor in the School of Nursing. Reporting to the Dean, the Visiting Professor of Nursing is a Spring 2027, non-tenure track position. This position will contribute to undergraduate nursing education with a focus on Medical Surgical Nursing. This role emphasizes excellence in teaching, student mentorship, and service to the university and surrounding community, while fostering a diverse and inclusive academic environment. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (including, but not limited to) : Essential duties: Teaching and Curriculum Development Design and deliver evidence-based teaching strategies for undergraduate nursing courses. Integrate innovative and inclusive pedagogical approaches into the curriculum. Student Engagement Mentor and advise nursing students to support academic and professional growth. Promote a culture of equity, inclusion, and academic freedom, fostering a welcoming environment for all students and colleagues. Service & Collaboration Participate in service activities within the university, School of Nursing, and local community. Collaborate with faculty and staff to support the mission and goals of the School of Nursing. Secondary Responsibilities: Support and foster interprofessional education and collaborative practice experiences. Engage in clinical practice as required by advanced practice certification. Provide optional volunteer opportunities at the Widener Community Nursing Clinic, offering pro bono care to underserved/uninsured populations. Perform other job-related duties as assigned or directed to support departmental needs and align with the mission of the School of Nursing. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (education/training and experience required) : Required: Master’s degree in Nursing (MSN). Degree must be from an accredited University or College. Active RN license and eligibility for licensure in Pennsylvania. Three (3+) years of academic teaching experience including clinical instruction. An equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered. Three (3+) years of professional experience in Medical Surgical Nursing. Demonstrated excellence in communication and collaboration. Preferred: Certification in Medical Surgical Nursing. Certification as a Nurse Educator (CNE), CNE Clinical, and/or CNE Novice. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND/OR UNUSUAL HOURS: Evening teaching assignments may be required. This position requires a commitment to academic excellence, innovation, and student success. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Widener University is committed to fostering an inclusive community in which faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. U.S. work authorization is required. Widener University, an independent, metropolitan, doctoral-intensive university, connects curricula to social issues through civic engagement. Dynamic teaching, active scholarship, personal attention and experiential learning are key components of the Widener Experience. Located in Chester, PA, Widener's main campus is nestled between Philadelphia, PA and Wilmington, DE, with Law Schools located in both Harrisburg and Wilmington. For more information about the university, please visit our website at www.widener.edu. EOE M/F/V/D Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.widener.edu/en-us/job/493456/visiting-associate-professor-of-law-delaware-law-school": {
      "title": "Visiting Associate Professor of Law - Delaware Law School",
      "description": "Visiting Associate Professor of Law - Delaware Law School Apply now Job no: 493456 Work type: Faculty (Non-tenure track) Location: Delaware Categories: Faculty Reporting to the Dean at the Delaware Law School, the Visiting Associate Professor of Law works as a full-time faculty member, teaching in both the fall and spring semesters of the academic year. This is a ten (10) month role for one academic year starting in Fall 2027-2028. Visiting Professors are valued members of our academic community who teach core or specialized legal courses, mentor Juris Doctor (JD) (and/or LL.M.) students, and enrich our intellectual life through active participation in faculty workshops and scholarship. The visiting professor is assigned to a temporary, non-tenure-track appointment. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (including, but not limited to): Essential Duties: Teaching : Teach two (2) law courses per semester in legal methods. Based on the visitor’s experience, there may be an opportunity to teach an additional course as an overload in the visitor’s area of expertise or core curriculum needs. Student Engagement : Hold regular office hours, mentor students, and evaluate student performance through exams, papers, or practical exercises. Scholarship : Participate in faculty speaker series, present work-in-progress papers, and engage in ongoing legal scholarship or writing during the appointment. Service : Participate selectively in faculty meetings, academic events, and student-facing institutional programs. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (education/training and experience required): Required: Juris Doctor (J.D.), LL.M., J.S.D., or an equivalent terminal law degree from an accredited institution. Degree must be from an accredited University or College. Demonstrated excellence or strong potential in teaching law to upper-level or foundational law students. A track record of or strong commitment to legal scholarship, practice experience, or prior academic appointments. Preferred: Current or former full-time law faculty status at another accredited law school (senior or junior level), or extensive distinguished practitioner/judicial clerkship experience. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Widener University is committed to fostering an inclusive community in which faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds, cultures, and personal experiences are welcomed and can thrive. We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. U.S. work authorization is required. Widener University, an independent, metropolitan, doctoral-intensive university, connects curricula to social issues through civic engagement. Dynamic teaching, active scholarship, personal attention and experiential learning are key components of the Widener Experience. Located in Chester, PA, Widener's main campus is nestled between Philadelphia, PA and Wilmington, DE, with Law Schools located in both Harrisburg and Wilmington. For more information about the university, please visit our website at www.widener.edu. EOE M/F/V/D Advertised: 30 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    }
